  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-af513933-9d43-47f8-98a0-12df5c9290f5-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "The original Overwatch was a team-based shooter in which players selected heroes with markedly different weapons, movement abilities, and support tools. Its six-player teams competed over objectives such as escorting a payload or holding territory. Choosing complementary heroes and adapting to the opposing team were as important as individual accuracy."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-af513933-9d43-47f8-98a0-12df5c9290f5-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Blizzard released the game in 2016 and expanded its roster and maps over time. This entry describes that original version; its live service was replaced by Overwatch 2 in 2022, so the original game’s team structure should not be confused with every later form of Overwatch."
    },
